    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`solution.py` implements `encode` and `decode` per `spec.md`, and `tests/test_solution.py` has 89 pytest tests, all passing with `python -m pytest -q tests`. `encode` groups runs with `itertools.groupby`. `decode` is split into small helpers, `_read_count` and `_read_run`, so each function's cyclomatic complexity stays well under 10, which keeps CRAP low. Digits are matched as ASCII `0`–`9` only, so Unicode digits are rejected. The tests cover the spec examples, the run-length boundaries (3, 4, 9, 10, 100), every `ValueError` case with its message, and round trips over fixed and seeded random inputs. I could not run coverage, mutation testing, or bandit, since the only permitted shell command was the test run. By reading the code, every line should be executed, and the error-message assertions should catch changes such as `0 <= ...` or `< 4` becoming `<= 4`. Decode does not cap counts, so a crafted input like `~999999999~a` will allocate a very large string; the spec does not mention a limit, so I left it alone.",
